Z||000000||sqoach||12-17-2001||03:32 PM||||Just sold my green coupe today. I got $1500 for it. I have mixed emotions, though. I needed to sell it, but wish I didn't have to. It was just having this overheating problem that I couldn't figure out. Though I did just replace the waterpump (again) and it's been ok since then. I was kinda sad when I saw it drive away.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>At least it's in good hands. The guy that bought it knows some stuff about them, and use to be a mechanic. Now I'm down to one fiero. I'm sure I'll get another one...someday  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>                 <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigsqoach2.gif">  <BR><B>86 SE V6 - daily driver</B><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><LI>86 Sport Coupe 2.5L 5spd (SOLD!)</FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||12-17-2001||05:00 PM||||Did you at least tell him about PFF?  I hope so!  One less fiero for you can mean one more member for us!<P>But I understand. I finally sold my 84SE that I bought when I was 15. It really wasn't worth restoring (rust kills, especially in Minnesota...especially after leaving it sit for 5 years).  But I still kinda hated to see it go.  It went to a good home (lowfierogt) and for a good cause (parts for him, AUS's Stage-2 for me).<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
